{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-tags-page-tsx","path":"/blog/tags/quick-thoughts/","result":{"data":{"tags":{"group":[{"fieldValue":"adventofcode","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"binary analysis","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"fuzzing","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"ghidra","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"linux","totalCount":3},{"fieldValue":"papers","totalCount":5},{"fieldValue":"pharos","totalCount":3},{"fieldValue":"programming","totalCount":4},{"fieldValue":"prolog","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"publications","totalCount":4},{"fieldValue":"quick thoughts","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"research","totalCount":6},{"fieldValue":"reverse engineering","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"rust","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"skiing","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"talks","totalCount":2},{"fieldValue":"travel","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"ubuntu","totalCount":1},{"fieldValue":"web","totalCount":3}]},"posts":{"totalCount":1,"edges":[{"node":{"htmlAst":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I saw a quote in a recent "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3630746"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"ACM article"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nthat resonated with me:"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"blockquote","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Security must be a business enabler, not a hinderer."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The article is about product development, but the quote is applicable to IT\nsecurity as well.  Too often, IT departments forget what their purpose is, which\nis "},{"type":"element","tagName":"em","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"to support the mission of the organization"}]},{"type":"text","value":".  Security is a means to that\nend, not an end in itself.  The goal of IT security is not to eliminate risk.\nThe most secure computer is one that is not plugged in, but that doesn't really\nhelp us, does it?  The goal of IT security is to manage risk so that the\norganization can achieve its mission. Unfortunately, it's significantly easier\nto just say \"No, you can't do that because it would increase our risk\" instead\nof \"Let me fully understand why you need or want to do that, have a discussion\nabout the security risks that will impose, and collaboratively make a decision\nthat balances the risks and rewards for the organization.\""}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I'm not saying that we should be cavalier about security.  After all, I'm\npersonally "},{"type":"element","tagName":"em","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"passionate"}]},{"type":"text","value":" about security.  But we should be "},{"type":"element","tagName":"em","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"intentional"}]},{"type":"text","value":" about\nhow and where we apply security when it impacts the mission, which is almost\nalways!"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I suspect a lot of people would be surprised at the (relatively low) level of\nsecurity I employ personally.  It's not that I'm lazy or incompetent.  It's that\nI've made a conscious decision to accept certain risks in order to achieve\ncertain rewards.  For example, I don't bother trying to defend against nation\nstate adversaries.  I'm not a high value target.  I don't have the resources\n(time) to defend against a nation state.  I'd rather be nimble and flexible in\nmy work capabilities, so I focus on the easy, low-hanging-fruit mitigations that\nwill stop most (but not all) attackers."}]}],"data":{"quirksMode":false}},"timeToRead":1,"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2024-02-25--quick-thoughts-security-must-be-a-business-enabler-not-a-hinderer/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["quick thoughts"],"title":"Quick Thoughts: \"Security must be a business enabler, not a hinderer.\"","updatedDate":"25 February, 2024","image":null,"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","bio":"Computer Security Researcher","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/83fe9/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/83fe9/ed.png 35w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/ad998/ed.png 70w","sizes":"35px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/dbb7e/ed.webp 35w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/299bc/ed.webp 70w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"35px"}]},"width":35,"height":35}}}}}}}]}},"pageContext":{"tag":"quick thoughts"}},"staticQueryHashes":[],"slicesMap":{}}